.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "BSDSF24A012-OS-A01" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrcpy
copies the null-terminated string from
.I src
to
.IR dest ,
including the terminating null character. The destination must have enough
space for the copied string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 if either pointer is NULL.
